> I was doing some benchmarking.  Then I noticed the alpha kept lousy time,
> then my cycle counter reported my clockspeed was off by 15% or so.
> 
> Then I noticed my clock is about 15% off.
> 
> I'm running 2.0.29, redhat-4.2 on a pws-433a
> 
> BogoMIPS                : 429.91  
> Linux pulsar.math.ucdavis.edu 2.0.29 #18 Wed Dec 31 18:19:25 PST 2014 alpha unknown      
> 
> Any ideas?

If you have a semi-perminant internet connection, you might want to
consider xntpd, a daemon that uses the Network Time Protocol to syncronize
your machine to various atomic clocks around the country, as well as
account for clock drift.  I have it on my cluster of UDBs, and it works
great.

