> the DU libXm.so does reside in /usr/shlib with appropriate permissions.
> Do I require a 2.1.X kernel to run DU 4.0 binaries?

In essence, yes.  Older kernels did not support all the hooks needed by
the DU 4.x libraries.  This was corrected when Linus started missing
Netscape on the Alpha, and tweaked the 2.1.x series to bring it up <g>.

I am not sure if the fixes propogated back to the 2.0.x kernels.

Steve

p.s. If worse comes to worse, the DU 3.x loader and libs do work on 2.0.x,
AFAIK.

